# Benchmark scorecards are COMMITTED: each one is a complete, self-contained measurement, and the
# model/rules-card verdict is derived from the whole corpus rather than from any single run. They
# cannot be "regenerated by re-running the benchmark" — most were produced by models whose weights
# have since been deleted, and re-running costs hours of GPU time to reproduce a number already
# known. What is NOT committed is the code each run produced: it is raw model output, frequently
# not valid Python, and every whole-repo analyzer that walks the tree would parse it and report a
# weak model's mistakes as this project's own. The scorecard records its style count instead, so
# the judgement survives without the files (`benchmarks/run.py --code-out`, pointed outside here).
benchmarks/scorecards/code-*/
.justdoit-in-progress
.diagnose-in-progress
